      <div id="childContent">
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 13986695"
      id="13986695"
      data-guid="13986695"
      data-position="64"
      data-full-title="SECTION 401: Common Council; Status and Title."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="13986695_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="13986695_label" for="13986695_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#13986695"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      SECTION 401
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="13986695"
    >
Common Council; Status and Title.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-13986695" data-guid="13986695"></div>
        <div id="questions-13986695" data-guid="13986695" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="13986695_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">The legislative power of the City is vested in the Common Council which shall be authorized to adopt, amend or repeal local laws, ordinances, resolutions and rules and regulations in the exercise of its functions, powers and duties pertaining to the property, affairs or government of the City and other matters not inconsistent with sate law.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 13986696"
      id="13986696"
      data-guid="13986696"
      data-position="65"
      data-full-title="SECTION 402: Members."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="13986696_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="13986696_label" for="13986696_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#13986696"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      SECTION 402
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="13986696"
    >
Members.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-13986696" data-guid="13986696"></div>
        <div id="questions-13986696" data-guid="13986696" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="13986696_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="history">[Amended at referendum <span class="legref" data-ref=""><span class="hisdate">11-2-2021</span></span>]</div><div class="para">The Common Council shall be an elective body comprised of a President of the Common Council and not more than one "Council member" duly elected from each ward within the City. Each "Council member" shall be a resident of the ward from which he or she is elected. There shall not be more than 15 wards within the City. All Common Council members shall be electors of the ward and have been residents continuously in the ward represented for at least 365 days prior to taking office. Each Common Council member shall reside in the ward from which that Common Council member seeks election at the time of nomination for office, and continue to be a resident of the ward for which he or she represents for his or her entire term of office, subject, however, to the following exception: in the case of an election immediately following the reapportionment of Common Council wards, the incumbent Common Council member representing a ward redrawn in such reapportionment shall be eligible for nomination for election in either the ward of residence, or any newly drawn district which is contiguous to the ward of residence, provided that the Common Council member shall become a resident of the ward represented prior to taking office. Common Council members shall be nominated at the primary election in the same manner other City officers are nominated pursuant to the provisions of the <a class="statref" href="https://municipal.codes/NY/ELN/" target="_blank">Election Law</a>.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 13986697"
      id="13986697"
      data-guid="13986697"
      data-position="66"
      data-full-title="SECTION 403: President of the Common Council."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="13986697_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="13986697_label" for="13986697_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#13986697"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      SECTION 403
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="13986697"
    >
President of the Common Council.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-13986697" data-guid="13986697"></div>
        <div id="questions-13986697" data-guid="13986697" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="13986697_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">The President of the Common Council shall be elected in the City at large, and shall succeed the Mayor in the event of death, resignation, absence or disability as set forth in the <a class="statref" href="https://municipal.codes/NY/GCT/" target="_blank">General City Law</a>; except that the powers and duties of the Office of the Mayor shall not devolve upon the President of the Common Council during a limited period of either absence of the Mayor from the City or inability of the Mayor to perform his or her powers and duties. The President shall preside over the meetings of the Common Council and perform such other functions as set forth in <a class="statref" href="https://municipal.codes/NY/SCC/" target="_blank">Second Class Cities Law</a>.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 13986698"
      id="13986698"
      data-guid="13986698"
      data-position="67"
      data-full-title="SECTION 404: Voting."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="13986698_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="13986698_label" for="13986698_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#13986698"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      SECTION 404
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="13986698"
    >
Voting.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-13986698" data-guid="13986698"></div>
        <div id="questions-13986698" data-guid="13986698" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="13986698_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">All legislation authorizing bond debt shall require a two-thirds vote of the entire Common Council membership. All other local laws, ordinances and resolutions shall require a majority vote of the entire Common Council membership, except as otherwise required by the <a class="statref" href="https://municipal.codes/NY/MHR/" target="_blank">Municipal Home Rule Law</a>. Public hearings on proposed local laws shall take place at the same time that public hearings are normally held on proposed ordinances.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 13986699"
      id="13986699"
      data-guid="13986699"
      data-position="68"
      data-full-title="SECTION 405: Filing and Publication of Local Laws; Judicial Notice."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="13986699_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="13986699_label" for="13986699_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#13986699"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      SECTION 405
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="13986699"
    >
Filing and Publication of Local Laws; Judicial Notice.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-13986699" data-guid="13986699"></div>
        <div id="questions-13986699" data-guid="13986699" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="13986699_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">The filing and publication of local laws shall be as provided in the <a class="statref" href="https://municipal.codes/NY/MHR/" target="_blank">Municipal Home Rule Law</a>.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 13986700"
      id="13986700"
      data-guid="13986700"
      data-position="69"
      data-full-title="SECTION 406: Reapportionment."
      data-code-content-type="section"
  >
    <span class="selectionBox material-icons material-symbols-outlined material-symbols-and-filled md-24"
         title="Select this content"
         aria-label="Select this content"
    >
      <input type="checkbox" class="selectionBoxInput" id="13986700_input"/>
    </span>
    <label class="selectionLabel" id="13986700_label" for="13986700_input">
  <div class="titleLinkContainer">
    <a href="#13986700"
       class="titleLink"
    >
    <span class="titleNumber">
      SECTION 406
    </span>
    <span class="titleTitle"
          data-guid="13986700"
    >
Reapportionment.    </span>
    </a>
  </div>
      </label>
  </div>
                </header>
        <div class="notes" id="notes-13986700" data-guid="13986700"></div>
        <div id="questions-13986700" data-guid="13986700" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="13986700_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="level"><div class="litem" id="13986701"><a alt="C-406(a)" class="litem_number" href="13986701#13986701" onclick="return false;" title="C-406(a)">(a) </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">Pursuant to the guidelines set forth in the <a class="statref" href="https://municipal.codes/NY/MHR/" target="_blank">Municipal Home Rule Law</a>, the Common Council shall appoint a reapportionment commission within six months after the publication of each federal decennial census to evaluate the existing ward boundaries for equity and representation in relation to population. The reapportionment commission shall include City residents in such proportion as to reasonably reflect the demographic composition of the City, together with such other expert and official representatives as shall be deemed necessary and appropriate.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="13986702"><a alt="C-406(b)" class="litem_number" href="13986702#13986702" onclick="return false;" title="C-406(b)">(b) </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">The reapportionment commission shall review the population data and within six months after the commission is appointed, make recommendations, if necessary, in the form of a proposed local law as to changes in the ward boundaries for the City.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div><div class="litem" id="13986703"><a alt="C-406(c)" class="litem_number" href="13986703#13986703" onclick="return false;" title="C-406(c)">(c) </a><div class="litem_content content"><div class="para">In its deliberations, the Commission shall consider the application of the "one person, one vote" concept and the equal protection clauses of the <a class="statref" href="https://municipal.codes/US/Const/Amendment14" target="_blank">Fourteenth</a> Amendment of the United States Constitution and Article <a class="xref" guid="13986636" href="13986636#13986636">I</a>, Sections I and II of the New York State Constitution.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div></div></div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 13986704"
