        <div class="notes" id="notes-13986704" data-guid="13986704"></div>
        <div id="questions-13986704" data-guid="13986704" class="questions"></div>


<div class="section_content content" id="13986704_content" title-footnotes="0"><div class="para">The Common Council may examine the books, vouchers and papers of any department, board, commission, officer or employee of the City and by the issuance of a subpoena, summon and examine under oath any person in relation thereto. The Common Council may require a member of any board, office, commission, or department of the City to furnish the Common Council with any information, data and reports; neglect or refusal to furnish the same shall be deemed misconduct or incompetence on the part of the official or person neglecting or refusing to comply. The authority conferred on the Common Council by this section shall not extend to the Mayor or the Office of the Mayor.</div><div class="footnotes"></div></div>                </article>
                <article>
                <header>
  <div data-component="h2"
       class="contentTitle barTitle sectionTitle 13986705"
